  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **at dawn** (1 review): The reviewer considered the actual performance of this song the evening's highlight [6]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **one big**: back after 29 archived shows (373 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [7]\n- **laylord**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **phone**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [7]\n- **i needed it most**: rare: 9 archived performances [7]\n- **way he brings**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **wordless**: rare: 5 archived performances [7]\n- **i will sing**: back after 29 archived shows (373 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2006-12-01.Electric_Factory_WXPN_FM_SBD** (recommended): soundboard; 20 songs; 119 min; rated 5/5 by 5 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer stood near soundboard until At Dawn, then moved to front [3]\n- Reviewer believes their hoarse voice is heard yelling before this song [3]\n- The At Dawn file contains only Jim James speaking, not the song [6]\n- This live performance is rated as being just as good as the DVD [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2006-12-01.Electric_Factory_WXPN_FM_SBD**: taped by Craig Taraszki; transferred by Craig Taraszki; source: FM/SBD> Sony PCM-R300 DAT (16/44.1, SBM) [1]. Also: Recorded via FM to Sony PCM-R300 DAT, then processed in Wave Lab; Tracks converted to CDWave and finally encoded as FLAC16 audio files [1]",
